config BR2_PACKAGE_VIGIL
	bool "vigil"
	# The platform's media stack, which the board's defconfig enables: a
	# vigil platform per osdrv package.
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_HISILICON_OSDRV_HI3536DV100 || \
		BR2_PACKAGE_SIGMASTAR_OSDRV_INFINITY2M
	depends on BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
	depends on !BR2_PACKAGE_MAJESTIC
	depends on !BR2_PACKAGE_VDEC_OPENIPC
	select BR2_PACKAGE_LIBYAML
	select BR2_PACKAGE_MBEDTLS_OPENIPC
	help
	  vigil - DVR/NVR application: network cameras (RTSP, NETIP,
	  ONVIF) decoded to HDMI/VGA with an on-screen UI (mouse and
	  keyboard), and recorded without re-encoding.

	  Installs /usr/bin/vigild, /etc/init.d/S95vigil (started at
	  boot and restarted after a crash, as majestic is) and
	  /etc/vigil.yaml, a YAML file like majestic's, which vigild
	  keeps itself: it rewrites it when settings change, with each
	  setting explained in a comment (comments written by hand are
	  not kept).

	  It listens, by default on every interface:
	    8080   HTTP/WebSocket API
	    80     zero channel: the screen, mouse and keyboard in a
	           browser (web.enabled)
	    554    RTSP: the cameras' streams (rtsp_server)
	    8899   ONVIF, and WS-Discovery on UDP 3702 (onvif_server)
	    34567  NETIP for XM's CMS/XMEye, and its search on UDP
	           34569 (netip_server)
	  Each logs in vigil's users (and root) and can be turned off or
	  moved in Network > Ports or vigil.yaml. None is encrypted: the
	  API's and the zero channel's passwords cross the network in
	  clear, as with a camera's web UI, so use them on a trusted
	  network or through an SSH tunnel. root cannot log in to any of
	  them while it has no password (an unclaimed image). The
	  passwords vigild keeps are sealed under /etc/vigil.key
	  (AES-256-GCM).

	  An /etc/vigil.json from an earlier image is converted into
	  vigil.yaml once, and kept as vigil.json.migrated. vigild records
	  only onto a mounted disk, card or share, never onto the flash or
	  into RAM, and starts recording by itself once the disk is there.

	  https://github.com/OpenIPC/vigil
